---
title: 'Range Controls'
enterprise: true
---

Range Controls allow the user to easily navigate to specific time periods and ranges along the chart timeline.

## Range Buttons

{% chartExampleRunner title="Range Buttons" name="range-buttons" type="generated" /%}

...

```js format="snippet"
{
    ranges: {
        enabled: true,
    }
}
```

## Custom Buttons

It is possible to override the default buttons by providing an array of button objects.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Custom Range Buttons" name="custom-range-buttons" type="generated" /%}

Custom buttons can be defined through the `ranges` options object.

```js format="snippet"
{
    ranges: {
        buttons: [
            { label: 'Teenagers', value: [15, 19] },
            { label: 'Young Adults', value: [20, 29] },
            { label: 'Middle Aged', value: [30, 65] },
            { label: 'Retired', value: (_start, end) => [66, end] },
            { label: 'All Ages', value: undefined },
        ],
    },
}
```

In this configuration:

-   `label` specifies the text displayed on the button.
-   `value` determines the time range the button applies:
    -   ...

